166c1a9, removed fixed timeout/bucket assumptions and validated dynamic parser, external-reality, and actor-routing repairs under a constant 6-worker pool)\n1518:- 0% hardcode, 6 workers, external-sources-timeout.ts, PULSE_EXTERNAL_SOURCES_TIMEOUT_MS, PULSE_EXECUTION_TRACE.json, parser-self-trust, live-vs-snapshot, capability-product-dynamic.spec.ts, actor-mode-dynamic.spec.ts, productionAutonomyVerdict NAO\n1520:## Task 11: Harden PULSE authority separation, runtime fusion, and shared-contract integration after parallel workers, outcome partial\n1524:- rollout_summaries/2026-04-29T18-42-47-KU5j-pulse_autonomy_workers_runtime_fusion_dod_parser_authority.md (cwd=/Users/danielpenin/whatsapp_saas, rollout_path=/Users/danielpenin/.codex/sessions/2026/04/29/rollout-2026-04-29T15-42-47-019dda8d-0134-7261-9044-13543bacfee9.jsonl, updated_at=2026-04-29T21:45:21+00:00, thread_id=019dda8d-0134-7261-9044-13543bacfee9, used parallel workers to harden runtime-fusion, DoD, blueprints, false-positive memory, parser/plugin discovery, and work-now vs declare-complete authority splits)\n1533:- when the user’s anti-gambiarra prompt is in scope -> prefer automated gates, strict lint/typecheck, and no \"quick fix\" casts or workflow bypasses [Task 2]\n1542:- when the user asks about \"infinitos agentes autonomos ... sem drift?\" -> define the safe model as governed cycles with one planner and bounded `ai_safe` workers, not unlimited parallel agents [Task 6]\n1546:- when the user says \"mantenha sempre 6 workers ativos... quando eles terminarem, voce cancela eles e dispara novos\" -> keep a fixed active-worker pool with explicit ownership slices and immediate worker recycling instead of serial batches [Task 10]\n1548:- when the user asks for maximum subagents on PULSE internals, assume one central integration pass is still required after worker-local wins; do not claim completion from one worker’s local `tsc`/Vitest success alone [Task 11]\n1554:- `KLOEL_STRICT_LINT=true` turns on `@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any`, but whole-repo strict lint surfaced too much legacy debt. Use diff-aware changed-hunk enforcement to block new abuse without bricking the repo [Task 1]\n1555:- `node scripts/ops/check-all-gates.mjs` became the broad integration check and passed governance-boundary, visual-contract, test-integrity, unsafe-casts, unsafe-queries, security, architecture, layer-boundaries, model-strings, code-quality, data-integrity, ratchet, lint, frontend-typecheck, backend-typecheck, worker-typecheck, and frontend-test before backend-test failed [Task 2]\n1557:- The repo has unusually strong process/ops scaffolding, but code-level rigor lagged: backend and worker had lenient TypeScript settings, frontend lint relaxed noisy rules, and large files/services/processors were maintainability hotspots [Task 3]\n1558:- Existing repo pattern uses mirrored contract files plus `scripts/ops/check-contract-sync.mjs`; extending that to backend-worker queue contracts was the low-risk governance move for `sweep-unread-conversations` [Task 3]\n1581:- After a parallel worker wave, expect the shared contract layer to be the first integration choke point. The high-signal repair loop is `npx tsc -p scripts/pulse/tsconfig.json --noEmit`, then the smallest relevant Vitest slice, then another `tsc` pass until `types.manifest.ts`, `contract-tester.ts`, `external-signals.ts`, and related shared surfaces converge [Task 11]\n1586:- Symptom: governance hardening blocks on hundreds of legacy `any` violations. Cause: whole-repo strict lint is too broad for current debt. Fix: enforce strictness on changed lines and ratchet/allowlist legacy debt explicitly [Task 1]\n1597:- Symptom: the user asks about \"infinite agents\" and the answer drifts into hype. Cause: the agent conflates continuous autonomy with unbounded concurrency. Fix: define the safe architecture as `PULSE -> planner -> N workers -> validation -> merge -> PULSE -> next cycle` with locks and isolated workspaces [Task 6]\n1604:- Symptom: a parallel worker rollout looks green locally but the full PULSE type layer is still broken. Cause: worker-local success hid shared-contract drift in `types.manifest.ts`, `contract-tester.ts`, `external-signals.ts`, or adjacent shared surfaces. Fix: reserve a central post-worker integration pass and do not treat one worker’s `tsc` as repo-wide proof [Task 11]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
